            <ArticleTitle>Bioptome-assisted coil occlusion of coronary artery fistula.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>189-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a novel technique that allows controlled and precise delivery of single or multiple coils simultaneously for occlusion of a coronary artery fistula using a bioptome passed via a long sheath positioned at the distal end of the fistula. The fistula was balloon occluded distal to the take-off of the native branches before, during and after coil delivery in two patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
